---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageGraphic from "../../components/PageGraphic.astro";
import "../../styles/about.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="I build production AI and the teams behind it. Ten years in software and the last five focused on production AI."
  active="about"
>
  <main>
    <PageGraphic page="about" />
    <article class="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
      <header class="about__head wrap wrap--read">
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--parts"><span class="eyebrow__part">AI Engineering Leader</span> <span class="eyebrow__part">Agentic&nbsp;Systems</span></p>
        <h1 id="about-title" class="about__title">Cristian <span class="highlight">Vega</span></h1>
        <p class="about__lede">I build production AI and the teams behind it.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="about__body wrap wrap--read">
        <div class="about__profile">
          <p>
            I’m an AI engineering leader at Vertafore with ten years in software and the last five focused on
            production AI. I’ve set strategy, owned budgets, and advised executives on responsible AI governance.
            Through it all, I’ve stayed hands-on: designing systems and writing production code.
          </p>
          <p>
            At Patra, I founded the AI Engineering function and grew it to a peak of ~50 people. We scaled
            document intelligence to 12,000 documents and more than 400,000 data points per month across 14+
            lines of business, with accuracy in the mid-90% range at $0.20 per document. I owned the budget, from
            the engineering organization down to the cost of a single policy check.
          </p>
          <p>
            That work reflects how I approach AI:
          </p>
          <ul class="about__principles">
            <li>Use deterministic execution where it does the job.</li>
            <li>Bring in models where reasoning is needed.</li>
            <li>Build reusable components rather than one-off pipelines.</li>
            <li>Clear system contracts, evaluation, and instrumentation belong in the design from the start.</li>
            <li>Quality should be measurable, and operating costs should be understood.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Nearly all of my career has been in regulated industries, including four and a half years building
            digital banking software at BBVA before moving into insurance. That experience taught me to treat
            compliance as part of the architecture, not a layer added after the system is built.
          </p>
          <p>
            Named inventor on U.S. Patent 12,639,972 B2.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
